  "description": "Greatest Hits is a compilation album by Tom Petty and the Heartbreakers, released on November 16, 1993. It is Petty's best-selling album to date and was certified 12× Platinum by the RIAA on April 28, 2015. The single \"Mary Jane's Last Dance\", one of two previously unreleased tracks on the album, became one of Petty's most popular songs, reaching No. 14 on the Billboard Hot 100 and No. 1 on the Billboard Mainstream Rock Tracks chart. The other new song on the album is a cover of the Thunderclap Newman hit \"Something in the Air\", which reached No. 19 on the Billboard Mainstream Rock Tracks chart. The album contains no songs from 1987's Let Me Up . However, three songs from Petty's 1989 solo album Full Moon Fever, along with four tracks from 1979's Damn the Torpedoes were included.",
